IMPORT prelude

-- Newfoundland and Labrador Income Tax Act, 2000 (SNL2000 cI-1.1), Part II -- the personal income tax of an individual,
-- for the 2025 and 2026 taxation years: who must pay (s 6(1)); the tax on taxable income (s 7, with the amounts as
-- indexed under s 6.1); the personal credits (s 9(1), (2), (3)); the CPP and EI credit (s 17); the low income reduction
-- (s 21.1); the order of the credits (s 23); and the income supplement and seniors' benefit (s 34 with the Income
-- Supplement and Seniors' Benefit Regulations, NLR 32/16). The s 34(8) duty to notify is in nl-pit-notice.l4.
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer. "Must I pay Newfoundland and Labrador income tax? How much? What credits do I get, and
-- what is paid back to me?" The Minister of National Revenue appears only as what the individual must tell, and by when.
--
-- Edition: the House of Assembly consolidation of the Act as amended to 2026 c15, retrieved 2026-10-24 (selected
-- sections deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SNL2000-cI-1.1-selected.txt); NLR 32/16 as amended to 17/26; NLR
-- 60/24. The bracket thresholds and credit amounts for 2025 and 2026 are not printed in the Act (s 6.1 indexes them each
-- year); they are taken from the Department of Finance's page, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/nl-finance-personalincometax.txt (NOTES.md findings 1 and 2).
--
-- Federal figures are inputs: taxable income, net income, the s 118.7 base for CPP and EI, the pension income amount
-- and adjusted income under ss 122.5 and 122.6 of the federal Act. Read with the federal Income Tax Act encoding,
-- subjects/ca/income-tax-act/ (cross-folder IMPORT is not possible in the stable l4).
--
-- NOT ENCODED (answers `not covered` where a question can reach it): taxation years other than 2025 and 2026; an
-- individual not resident in the province on the last day of the year (s 6(1)(b), ss 25, 31); trusts; every credit not
-- listed above (ss 10 to 16, 17.1 to 21, 33, 45.1 to 47); minimum tax (s 30) and tax on split income (s 29); the
-- Newfoundland and Labrador child benefit (s 38).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Newfoundland and Labrador Income Tax Act, 2000 -- the personal income tax of an individual`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `only the 2025 and 2026 taxation years are encoded`
    `only an individual resident in the province on the last day of the taxation year is encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `taxation year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the taxation year is encoded` IF
    `taxation year` EQUALS 2025 OR `taxation year` EQUALS 2026

§§ `Small arithmetic`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`zero or more` x MEANS IF x GREATER THAN 0 THEN x ELSE 0

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` x y MEANS IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the cent` x MEANS (ROUND (x TIMES 100)) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `s 6(1) -- who must pay`

-- s 6(1): "An income tax shall be paid as required by this Act for each taxation year by every individual (a) who was
-- resident in the province on the last day of the taxation year; or (b) who, not being resident in the province on the
-- last day of the taxation year, had income earned in the taxation year in the province." Residence is a borrowed
-- (federal, common-law) term, asked as a fact. "Individual" includes a trust (s 2(1)(i)); trusts are not encoded.
GIVEN `resident in the province on the last day of the taxation year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had income earned in the taxation year in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual must pay income tax under the Act` IF
        `resident in the province on the last day of the taxation year`
    OR  `had income earned in the taxation year in the province`

§§ `s 7 and s 6.1 -- the tax on taxable income`

-- s 7(1) sets eight rates on "taxable income" (the federal taxable income, s 5 and s 2(1)): 8.7%, 14.5%, 15.8%, 17.8%,
-- 19.8%, 20.8%, 21.3% and 21.8%, each on the part of taxable income above the previous threshold. The thresholds printed
-- in s 7(1) ($38,081; $76,161; $135,973; $190,363; $250,000; $500,000; $1,000,000) are the 2022 base; s 7(2), (3) and
-- s 6.1 index every one of them each year by the provincial CPI, rounded to the nearest dollar. The indexed thresholds
-- are not in the Act: they are the Department of Finance's figures for 2025 and 2026.
DECLARE `Bracket thresholds` HAS
    `first`   IS A NUMBER
    `second`  IS A NUMBER
    `third`   IS A NUMBER
    `fourth`  IS A NUMBER
    `fifth`   IS A NUMBER
    `sixth`   IS A NUMBER
    `seventh` IS A NUMBER

-- The thresholds as printed in s 7(1) (the 2022 base, before indexation).
`the thresholds printed in s 7(1)` MEANS
    `Bracket thresholds` WITH
        `first`   IS 38081
        `second`  IS 76161
        `third`   IS 135973
        `fourth`  IS 190363
        `fifth`   IS 250000
        `sixth`   IS 500000
        `seventh` IS 1000000

-- Department of Finance, "Personal Income Tax", 2025 column.
`the 2025 thresholds` MEANS
    `Bracket thresholds` WITH
        `first`   IS 44192
        `second`  IS 88382
        `third`   IS 157792
        `fourth`  IS 220910
        `fifth`   IS 282214
        `sixth`   IS 564429
        `seventh` IS 1128858

-- Department of Finance, "Personal Income Tax", 2026 column.
`the 2026 thresholds` MEANS
    `Bracket thresholds` WITH
        `first`   IS 44678
        `second`  IS 89354
        `third`   IS 159528
        `fourth`  IS 223340
        `fifth`   IS 285319
        `sixth`   IS 570638
        `seventh` IS 1141275

GIVEN `taxation year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Bracket thresholds`
`the thresholds for the year` `taxation year` MEANS
    IF `taxation year` EQUALS 2025 THEN `the 2025 thresholds` ELSE `the 2026 thresholds`

-- The part of taxable income that falls between a lower and an upper threshold.
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER, `lower` IS A NUMBER, `upper` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the slice of` `taxable income` `between` `lower` `and` `upper` MEANS
    `zero or more` ((`the lesser of` `taxable income` `upper`) MINUS `lower`)

-- s 7(1)(a) to (h): each paragraph is "the maximum amount determinable ... under" the one before "plus" its rate on the
-- excess over its threshold, which is the sum of each rate on its own slice.
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER, t IS A `Bracket thresholds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 7 tax on` `taxable income` `with thresholds` t MEANS
      (8.7%  TIMES (`the slice of` `taxable income` `between` 0 `and` (t's `first`)))
    + (14.5% TIMES (`the slice of` `taxable income` `between` (t's `first`) `and` (t's `second`)))
    + (15.8% TIMES (`the slice of` `taxable income` `between` (t's `second`) `and` (t's `third`)))
    + (17.8% TIMES (`the slice of` `taxable income` `between` (t's `third`) `and` (t's `fourth`)))
    + (19.8% TIMES (`the slice of` `taxable income` `between` (t's `fourth`) `and` (t's `fifth`)))
    + (20.8% TIMES (`the slice of` `taxable income` `between` (t's `fifth`) `and` (t's `sixth`)))
    + (21.3% TIMES (`the slice of` `taxable income` `between` (t's `sixth`) `and` (t's `seventh`)))
    + (21.8% TIMES (`zero or more` (`taxable income` MINUS (t's `seventh`))))

-- s 5(a): "appropriate percentage" for a taxation year means the lowest percentage referred to in section 7: 8.7%.
`the appropriate percentage` MEANS 8.7%

§§ `s 9 -- personal credits`

-- The s 9 amounts for 2025 and 2026, as published by the Department of Finance (indexed under s 6.1; s 9(5) holds the
-- $13,094 of s 9(1)(a)(i), (b)(iii) and (c) unindexed before 2027, so 2026 is the printed figure). The income
-- thresholds inside the s 9(1)(a), (b) and s 9(2) formulas ($606 and $33,226 in the text) are indexed too but are not on
-- the Finance page, so they are inputs (NOTES.md finding 3).
DECLARE `Credit amounts` HAS
    `basic personal amount`              IS A NUMBER
    `age amount`                         IS A NUMBER
    `spouse or eligible dependant amount` IS A NUMBER

`the 2025 credit amounts` MEANS
    `Credit amounts` WITH
        `basic personal amount`               IS 11067
        `age amount`                          IS 7064
        `spouse or eligible dependant amount` IS 9043

`the 2026 credit amounts` MEANS
    `Credit amounts` WITH
        `basic personal amount`               IS 13094
        `age amount`                          IS 7142
        `spouse or eligible dependant amount` IS 9142

GIVEN `taxation year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Credit amounts`
`the credit amounts for the year` `taxation year` MEANS
    IF `taxation year` EQUALS 2025 THEN `the 2025 credit amounts` ELSE `the 2026 credit amounts`

-- Which paragraph of s 9(1) the individual claims under: (a) a married person or common law partner who supports a
-- spouse or partner and is not living apart because of a breakdown; (b) an unmarried (or separated, unsupported) person
-- who maintains a home in which they support a related, wholly dependent person (the "eligible dependant"); (c)
-- everyone else. Whether (a) or (b) applies is a borrowed set of facts, asked as a choice.
DECLARE `s 9(1) claim` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (a) -- supporting a spouse or common law partner`
    `paragraph (b) -- supporting an eligible dependant`
    `paragraph (c) -- the basic amount only`

-- s 9(1)(a)(ii): "$6,055 - (C - $606) where C is the greater of $606 and the income of the individual's spouse or common
-- law partner for the year"; (b)(iv) the same with D, the dependent person's income. $6,055 and $606 are the printed base
-- figures; the indexed maximum and threshold are used. The text has no "if any": a dependant whose income exceeds the
-- maximum plus the threshold would give a negative amount, which the encoding treats as nil (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `maximum` IS A NUMBER, `threshold` IS A NUMBER, `the other person's income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the spouse or dependant part` MEANS
    LET c MEANS IF `the other person's income` GREATER THAN `threshold` THEN `the other person's income` ELSE `threshold`
    IN  `zero or more` (`maximum` MINUS (c MINUS `threshold`))

-- s 9(1): the amount B. Under (a) and (b) it is the total of the basic amount and the spouse or dependant part; under (c)
-- it is the basic amount.
GIVEN `claim` IS A `s 9(1) claim`, amounts IS A `Credit amounts`, `threshold` IS A NUMBER, `the other person's income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 9(1) amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `claim`
    WHEN `paragraph (c) -- the basic amount only` THEN amounts's `basic personal amount`
    OTHERWISE amounts's `basic personal amount`
              PLUS `the spouse or dependant part` (amounts's `spouse or eligible dependant amount`) `threshold` `the other person's income`

-- s 9(2): an individual who "before the end of the year, has attained the age of 65 years" may deduct
-- "A x ($6,063 - B)" where B "is 15% of the amount, if any, by which the individual's income for the year would exceed
-- $33,226" (both indexed). As with s 9(1), a negative result is treated as nil.
GIVEN `65 or over before the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `maximum` IS A NUMBER
      `threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual's income for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 9(2) amount` MEANS
    IF `65 or over before the end of the year`
    THEN `zero or more` (`maximum` MINUS (15% TIMES (`zero or more` (`the individual's income for the year` MINUS `threshold`))))
    ELSE 0

-- s 9(3): an individual "resident in the province on the last day of the taxation year" may deduct "A x B" where B "is
-- the lesser of (a) $1,000; and (b) the amount determined under paragraph (b) of the description of B in subsection
-- 118(3) of the federal Act" (the federal pension income amount base). The $1,000 is not indexed (s 6.1(3)(b) lists only
-- subsections 9(1) and (2)).
GIVEN `the federal pension income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 9(3) amount` MEANS `the lesser of` 1000 (`zero or more` `the federal pension income amount`)

§§ `s 17 -- CPP contributions and EI premiums`

-- s 17: "Section 118.7 of the federal Act applies for the purpose of this Act", with the provincial appropriate
-- percentage. The amount the percentage is applied to (the employee's base CPP contributions and EI premiums, as the
-- federal section counts them) is an input.
GIVEN `the s 118.7 base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 17 credit` MEANS `the appropriate percentage` TIMES (`zero or more` `the s 118.7 base`)

§§ `s 23 -- the credits in order, and the tax after them`

-- s 23(2) applies s 9(1) and (2), then s 17, then s 9(3), ... and s 21.1 last. Each credit is a deduction from the tax
-- under s 7 and none is refundable, so the order matters only in that the tax cannot go below nil and s 21.1 comes after
-- the others (s 21.1(5)).
GIVEN `s 7 tax` IS A NUMBER, `s 9 and s 17 credits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax after the personal credits` MEANS `zero or more` (`s 7 tax` MINUS `s 9 and s 17 credits`)

§§ `s 21.1 -- the low income reduction`

-- s 21.1(2): "the amount, if any, by which A + B exceeds 16% of the amount, if any, by which (a) the eligible
-- individual's adjusted income for the year; exceeds (b) $18,547; or (c) where the eligible individual has a qualified
-- relation for the year or claims an amount under paragraph 9(1)(b) for the year, $31,362, may be deducted from the tax
-- otherwise payable". A is prescribed by regulation; B is prescribed and applies only with a qualified relation or a
-- s 9(1)(b) claim (s 21.1(2.1)). The thresholds are indexed (s 6.1(3)(b)). "Eligible individual": not a trust, resident
-- in the province on 31 December (s 21.1(1)(b)). "Adjusted income": the individual's and qualified relation's incomes
-- under s 122.6 of the federal Act.
GIVEN `eligible individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has a qualified relation or claims under s 9(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
      `amount A` IS A NUMBER
      `amount B` IS A NUMBER
      `single threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `family threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 21.1 reduction` MEANS
    IF `eligible individual`
    THEN LET `A plus B` MEANS IF `has a qualified relation or claims under s 9(1)(b)` THEN `amount A` PLUS `amount B` ELSE `amount A`
             `threshold` MEANS IF `has a qualified relation or claims under s 9(1)(b)` THEN `family threshold` ELSE `single threshold`
         IN  `zero or more` (`A plus B` MINUS (16% TIMES (`zero or more` (`adjusted income` MINUS `threshold`))))
    ELSE 0

-- NLR 60/24 s 3: for the 2024 taxation year, A is $974 and B is $544. No regulation for 2025 or 2026 was found in the
-- register's table of regulations under the Act on 2026-10-24 (NOTES.md finding 5).
`A for 2024 under NLR 60/24` MEANS 974
`B for 2024 under NLR 60/24` MEANS 544

-- The reduction is "deducted from the tax otherwise payable", which cannot go below nil.
GIVEN `tax after the personal credits` IS A NUMBER, `reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax after the low income reduction` MEANS `zero or more` (`tax after the personal credits` MINUS `reduction`)

§§ `s 34 and NLR 32/16 -- the income supplement and seniors' benefit`

-- s 34(3): an eligible individual "who files a return of income for the taxation year is considered to have paid during
-- the specified month on account of [their] tax payable ... an amount equal to 25% of the amount, if any, calculated in
-- accordance with the regulations". The specified months are "July and October of the immediately following taxation
-- year and January and April of the second immediately following taxation year" (s 34(12)). "Eligible individual",
-- "qualified relation", "qualified dependant" and "adjusted income" are the federal GST/HST credit terms (s 122.5 of the
-- federal Act), asked as facts.
--
-- NLR 32/16 s 3(a): "the amount by which the total of (i) $254, (ii) the lesser of $266 and 5.32% of the amount by
-- which the individual's adjusted income for the taxation year exceeds $15,000, (iii) $69 for the qualified relation,
-- if any, ... and (iv) the product obtained when $231 is multiplied by the number of qualified dependents ... exceeds (v)
-- 9% of the amount by which the individual's adjusted income for the taxation year exceeds $40,000".
GIVEN `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER, `has a qualified relation` IS A BOOLEAN, `qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income supplement` MEANS
    `zero or more`
        (   (254
             PLUS (`the lesser of` 266 (5.32% TIMES (`zero or more` (`adjusted income` MINUS 15000))))
             PLUS (IF `has a qualified relation` THEN 69 ELSE 0)
             PLUS (231 TIMES `qualified dependants`))
         MINUS (9% TIMES (`zero or more` (`adjusted income` MINUS 40000))))

-- s 3(b): "$231 where the individual is eligible to claim an amount under subsection 118.3(1) of the federal Act" (the
-- disability tax credit), and $231 where the qualified relation is, less "1.4% of the amount by which the individual's
-- adjusted income ... exceeds $29,402".
GIVEN `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER, `individual eligible for the disability tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN, `qualified relation eligible for the disability tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the disability amount` MEANS
    `zero or more`
        (   ((IF `individual eligible for the disability tax credit` THEN 231 ELSE 0)
             PLUS (IF `qualified relation eligible for the disability tax credit` THEN 231 ELSE 0))
         MINUS (1.4% TIMES (`zero or more` (`adjusted income` MINUS 29402))))

-- s 3(c): $1,882 "for an eligible individual who is 64 years of age or over at any time in the taxation year" (one
-- amount whether or not there is a qualified relation), less "11.66% of the amount by which the individual's adjusted
-- income ... exceeds $30,409". s 3.1: the s 3(c) amounts are indexed under s 6.1(2) of the Act, but not for 2026.
GIVEN `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER, `64 or over at any time in the taxation year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the seniors' benefit` MEANS
    IF `64 or over at any time in the taxation year`
    THEN `zero or more` (1882 MINUS (11.66% TIMES (`zero or more` (`adjusted income` MINUS 30409))))
    ELSE 0

-- The yearly total under s 3 and the amount for each specified month under s 34(3) (25%). s 34(10), (11): where each
-- monthly amount would be under $10, the whole year's total is paid in the first specified month.
GIVEN `yearly total` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each specified month's amount` MEANS `to the cent` (25% TIMES `yearly total`)

GIVEN `yearly total` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid in one amount in the first specified month` IF
        `yearly total` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (25% TIMES `yearly total`) LESS THAN 10
